1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,033
200,000+ MILES FROM EARTH, THEY HEARD A BANG

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:06,954
THEIR SPACECRAFT WAS DYING

3
00:00:07,204 --> 00:00:08,915
THE MOON LANDING WAS CANCELED

4
00:00:09,165 --> 00:00:11,764
NOW THE ONLY GOAL WAS GETTING HOME ALIVE

5
00:00:12,364 --> 00:00:13,883
THIS IS APOLLO 13

6
00:00:14,183 --> 00:00:17,273
IT LAUNCHED ON APRIL 11, 1970

7
00:00:17,523 --> 00:00:20,353
IT WAS MEANT TO BE NASA'S THIRD MOON LANDING

8
00:00:20,753 --> 00:00:24,237
THE CREW: LOVELL, HAISE, AND SWIGERT

9
00:00:24,487 --> 00:00:27,130
SWIGERT JOINED JUST DAYS BEFORE LAUNCH

10
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:31,920
ANOTHER ASTRONAUT WAS EXPOSED TO GERMAN MEASLES

11
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:35,022
TWO DAYS IN, EVERYTHING WAS GOING PERFECTLY

12
00:00:35,622 --> 00:00:40,733
THEN, ON APRIL 13, DAMAGED WIRING SPARKED INSIDE AN OXYGEN TANK

13
00:00:41,033 --> 00:00:42,313
THE TANK EXPLODED

14
00:00:42,713 --> 00:00:44,898
OXYGEN BEGAN LEAKING INTO SPACE

15
00:00:45,248 --> 00:00:49,250
“HOUSTON, WE'VE HAD A PROBLEM”

16
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,928
POWER WAS FAILING. THE OXYGEN WAS ALMOST GONE

17
00:00:54,528 --> 00:00:57,351
SO THE CREW DID SOMETHING NOBODY PLANNED FOR

18
00:00:57,651 --> 00:01:00,374
THEY MOVED INTO THE LUNAR MODULE, AQUARIUS

19
00:01:00,674 --> 00:01:03,424
BUILT TO KEEP 2 MEN ALIVE FOR 2 DAYS

20
00:01:03,724 --> 00:01:06,207
NOW IT HAD TO KEEP 3 MEN ALIVE FOR 4

21
00:01:06,607 --> 00:01:09,356
THEY SHUT DOWN ALMOST EVERYTHING TO SAVE POWER

22
00:01:09,656 --> 00:01:12,134
IT GREW BITTERLY COLD, CLOSE TO FREEZING

23
00:01:12,434 --> 00:01:14,078
WATER WAS STRICTLY RATIONED

24
00:01:14,678 --> 00:01:19,935
MISSION CONTROL USED THE MOON'S GRAVITY TO SWING THEM HOME

25
00:01:20,235 --> 00:01:22,414
THEY LOOPED AROUND THE FAR SIDE OF THE MOON

26
00:01:22,714 --> 00:01:25,547
FARTHER FROM EARTH THAN ANY HUMANS HAVE EVER BEEN

27
00:01:26,147 --> 00:01:29,095
THEN A NEW DANGER APPEARED: CARBON DIOXIDE

28
00:01:29,395 --> 00:01:31,838
THE LUNAR MODULE'S FILTERS WERE FILLING UP

29
00:01:32,138 --> 00:01:35,711
THE SPARE FILTERS WERE THE WRONG SHAPE

30
00:01:36,061 --> 00:01:41,211
ENGINEERS ON THE GROUND HAD TO INVENT AN ADAPTER

31
00:01:41,511 --> 00:01:44,592
A PLASTIC BAG, CARDBOARD, A HOSE, AND DUCT TAPE

32
00:01:44,942 --> 00:01:48,902
MISSION CONTROL READ THE STEPS. THE CREW BUILT IT

33
00:01:49,252 --> 00:01:50,016
IT WORKED

34
00:01:50,616 --> 00:01:55,089
THE GROUND TEAM WROTE A PLAN TO RESTART THE COLD COMMAND MODULE

35
00:01:55,389 --> 00:02:00,178
KEN MATTINGLY, THE GROUNDED ASTRONAUT, TESTED IT IN A SIMULATOR

36
00:02:00,528 --> 00:02:04,441
BEFORE REENTRY, THE CREW LET GO OF THE DAMAGED SERVICE MODULE

37
00:02:04,741 --> 00:02:07,531
AN ENTIRE PANEL HAD BEEN BLOWN AWAY

38
00:02:08,131 --> 00:02:11,254
THEN CAME REENTRY, AND THE RADIO WENT SILENT

39
00:02:11,554 --> 00:02:14,330
IT STAYED SILENT LONGER THAN ANYONE EXPECTED

40
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:16,167
MISSION CONTROL WAITED

41
00:02:16,667 --> 00:02:18,957
THEN, FINALLY, THE PARACHUTES OPENED

42
00:02:19,557 --> 00:02:23,965
ON APRIL 17, APOLLO 13 SPLASHED DOWN IN THE PACIFIC

43
00:02:24,315 --> 00:02:26,226
ALL 3 ASTRONAUTS WERE ALIVE

44
00:02:26,626 --> 00:02:28,744
NASA CALLED IT A “SUCCESSFUL FAILURE”

45
00:02:29,244 --> 00:02:33,351
NEXT: 13 TRAPPED IN A FLOODED CAVE. FOLLOW

